  "reason": "The current best result is config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.619 acc, and the only fusion strategy tested so far is concat. Config_019 is a single-variable ablation that swaps concat for weighted fusion while holding every other parameter identical to config_018. This directly tests whether learned modality weighting (vs. simple concatenation) improves the fusion of the two modalities, which is a fundamental design decision that will inform all future multimodal experiments. Given that aggregation choice already showed a ~4pp impact (avgpool vs. transformer), fusion strategy is a comparably important untested axis. Selecting config_019 is the most efficient exploitation of the strongest evidence: it either improves on the current best or confirms concat is sufficient, reducing uncertainty about the fusion design choice with minimal confounding."
